# Link Check Before Push

**Before any `git push` (or marking ship/PR ready):** always audit and fix link issues introduced or touched by the change.

## What to check

- Internal routes: `href`, `Link`, `router.push` / `replace`, redirects, CTA targets
- Admin + marketing nav items match real App Router pages
- Query/filter deep links (`categoryId`, `subcategoryId`, bank scopes) still resolve
- API client paths under `/api/v1` match controllers (no stale endpoints)
- Docs / README / runbook URLs that point into this repo
- Homepage / footer / empty-state CTAs after renames or removed pages

## How to verify

1. Grep changed files for `href=`, `push(`, `replace(`, and hardcoded path strings
2. Confirm each path exists under `frontend/src/app/` (or intentional external URL)
3. Confirm scope isolation: Written links stay on Written routes; Preli on Preli
4. Fix broken links in the same change set — do not push knowing links 404

## Do not

- Push with known dead nav/CTA links “to fix later”
- Leave old paths after page moves (e.g. removed dropdown targets, renamed admin routes)
